# 10. FINANCIAL CALCULATION ENGINE

Use decimal.js or integer minor units.

Avoid floating-point currency errors.

Definitions:

Scheduled Rent = Sum of Valid Rent Charges for Selected Period

Collected Rent = Sum of Valid Allocated Rent Payments

Outstanding Rent = Valid Rent Charges − Allocated Payments − Applicable Credits

Collection Rate = Collected Rent / Eligible Rent Charges × 100

Operating Cash Flow = Actual Cash Receipts − Actual Paid Operating Expenses

Occupancy Rate = Occupied Leasable Units / Total Eligible Leasable Units × 100

Handle zero denominators.

Security deposits must not be counted as rental revenue.

Reversals must not be double-counted.

Clearly distinguish rent charges, receivables, deposits, and cash collections.

This application is not a full double-entry accounting system.

